erent common-use idioms", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-02T16:50:42Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "7 questions, +10, no negs", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-02T16:51:06Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "##quiz start", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-02T16:51:54Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "1. During medieval times, when a guest had overstayed their welcome at a feast, the host wouldn't rudely kick them out. Instead, they would stop serving the hot, choice cuts of roasted meat. What specific, less-desirable cut of meat would they serve the guest to signal it was time to leave?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-02T16:52:07Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Cold shoulder", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-02T16:52:07Z", "username": "Nikhil Borra", "text": "Cold shoulder", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-02T16:52:22Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Correct. A cold shoulder of mutton (or beef). It was a polite, culinary way of saying, \"The party is over; go home.\"", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-02T16:52:44Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Vats 10", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]